{"beat": 11, "name": "ROSENWALD AND THE CATALOGUE", "text": "Richard Sears was a born copywriter. Make a watch sell a watch, he said. Roebuck, worn out, sold his stake. In 1895, a Chicago clothing man named Julius Rosenwald and his brother-in-law bought in, paying $75,000 for half the company. Sears wrote the catalogue. Rosenwald ran the business. By the turn of the century, with more than $10 million a year in sales, Sears had passed Montgomery Ward. The catalogue was a thick book, mailed to farms, selling everything from a stove to a buggy, and every item in it had to get from a building in Chicago to a door that might be across the continent.", "provider": "placeholder", "words": [{"word": "Richard", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.26}, {"word": "Sears", "start": 0.26, "end": 0.82}, {"word": "was", "start": 0.82, "end": 1.04}, {"word": "a", "start": 1.04, "end": 1.22}, {"word": "born", "start": 1.22, "end": 1.48}, {"word": "copywriter.", "start": 1.48, "end": 2.26}, {"word": "Make", "start": 2.76, "end": 2.94}, {"word": "a", "start": 2.94, "end": 3.1}, {"word": "watch", "start": 3.1, "end": 3.4}, {"word": "sell", "start": 3.58, "end": 3.72}, {"word": "a", "start": 3.72, "end": 3.84}, {"word": "watch,", "start": 3.84, "end": 4.2}, {"word": "he", "start": 4.36, "end": 4.44}, {"word": "said.", "start": 4.44, "end": 4.74}, {"word": "Roebuck,", "start": 5.34, "end": 5.8}, {"word": "worn", "start": 6.22, "end": 6.4}, {"word": "out,", "start": 6.4, "end": 6.68}, {"word": "sold", "start": 6.92, "end": 7.14}, {"word": "his", "start": 7.14, "end": 7.38}, {"word": "stake.", "start": 7.38, "end": 7.66}, {"word": "In", "start": 8.32, "end": 8.46}, {"word": "1895,", "start": 8.46, "end": 10.2}, {"word": "a", "start": 10.8, "end": 10.92}, {"word": "Chicago", "start": 10.92, "end": 11.3}, {"word": "clothing", "start": 11.3, "end": 11.82}, {"word": "man", "start": 11.82, "end": 12.3}, {"word": "named", "start": 12.3, "end": 12.66}, {"word": "Julius", "start": 12.66, "end": 13.16}, {"word"